1. **A sealing valve arrangement for a shaft furnace charging installation**, comprising:

a shutter configured to selectively close a material passage of the charging installation;

a valve seat arranged around the material passage and configured to sealingly cooperate with the shutter in a closed position of the sealing valve arrangement;

a dual-motion actuator operatively connected to the shutter and configured to move the shutter by a first motion and a second motion different from the first motion;

an eccentric sleeve shaft coupled to the shutter and configured to generate the first motion as a primary release motion, wherein rotation of the eccentric sleeve shaft displaces the shutter relative to the valve seat so as to release the shutter from sealing engagement with the valve seat; and

a tilting shaft carrying a tilting arm connected to the shutter, the tilting shaft and tilting arm being configured to generate the second motion as a secondary opening motion, wherein rotation of the tilting shaft pivots the tilting arm to move the shutter away from the material passage after the primary release motion,

wherein the dual-motion actuator is configured to coordinate the eccentric sleeve shaft and the tilting shaft such that, during opening of the sealing valve arrangement, the eccentric sleeve shaft first moves the shutter substantially out of sealing contact with the valve seat, and the tilting shaft subsequently moves the shutter into an open position offset from the material passage.

1. A sealing valve for a bell-less top furnace, comprising:  

a valve housing defining a material passage;  

a valve seat disposed in the material passage;  

a shutter configured to cooperate with the valve seat to selectively seal the material passage;  

a stationary cylindrical sleeve fixed relative to the valve housing and extending along a sleeve axis;  

an eccentric sleeve shaft rotatably received within the stationary cylindrical sleeve, the eccentric sleeve shaft defining an eccentric axis offset from the sleeve axis and being rotatable relative to the stationary cylindrical sleeve to impart a primary displacement to the shutter toward and away from alignment with the valve seat; and  

a tilting shaft rotatably received within the eccentric sleeve shaft and operatively connected to the shutter, the tilting shaft being rotatable relative to the eccentric sleeve shaft to impart a secondary tilting movement to the shutter relative to the valve seat;  

wherein rotation of the eccentric sleeve shaft produces a first component of movement of the shutter and rotation of the tilting shaft produces a second component of movement of the shutter, the first and second components of movement cooperating to move the shutter between an open position spaced from the valve seat and a closed position in sealing engagement with the valve seat.
